From: vigaz <pudimdebacon3@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:00:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Fix GPU frequency lock never reaching the kernel node

AxKernelManagerService registered each control's Settings.Secure
ContentObserver exactly once, inside systemReady(). Late-appearing
vendor procfs nodes (MediaTek gpufreqv2, unlike the early-available
generic cpufreq policies) are not guaranteed to exist yet at that
point, so the GPU frequency-lock control silently never got an
observer: Settings.Secure writes (from the UI, or even a raw
'settings put') persisted fine, but nothing ever wrote the real
sysfs/procfs node - confirmed live on device, including bypassing the
UI entirely with a direct settings put.

CPU controls were unaffected since their nodes are always present by
systemReady() time. The UI itself masked the bug further: it always
re-discovers all controls fresh via refreshControlsLocked() whenever
the Kernel Manager screen opens, so the slider always rendered with
correct values even though writes silently went nowhere.

Fix: make observer registration idempotent (tracked by Uri, so a
control can safely be (re)observed on every refresh) and register from
inside refreshControlsLocked() itself, which already runs on every
getControls() call - so opening the Kernel Manager screen is now
enough to pick up late-appearing nodes.

Investigated with a second opinion from Gemini before implementing.

Change-Id: I5e05afbf3c19fa11a8a86b99e9a02f338b97f52c
---
 .../server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java        | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ax_km_server/src/com/android/server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java b/ax_km_server/src/com/android/server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java
index 1188d39..5f0264a 100644
--- a/ax_km_server/src/com/android/server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java
+++ b/ax_km_server/src/com/android/server/kernel/AxKernelManagerService.java
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ import android.os.UserHandle;
 import android.provider.Settings;
 import android.text.TextUtils;
 import android.util.ArrayMap;
+import android.util.ArraySet;
 import android.util.Slog;
 
 import com.android.internal.kernel.AxKernelControl;
@@ -59,6 +60,13 @@ public final class AxKernelManagerService {
     private final Object mLock = new Object();
     private final ContentResolver mResolver;
     private final ArrayMap<String, KernelControlNode> mControls = new ArrayMap<>();
+    // Observers are registered lazily as controls are discovered (see
+    // refreshControlsLocked()), since some vendor sysfs/procfs nodes (e.g.
+    // MediaTek's gpufreqv2) aren't ready yet at systemReady() time. Tracked
+    // here so re-registering on every refresh doesn't double-register the
+    // same Uri (ContentResolver does not dedupe that itself - it would fire
+    // onChange() once per registration).
+    private final ArraySet<Uri> mObservedUris = new ArraySet<>();
     private final AxKernelMetricsReader mMetricsReader = new AxKernelMetricsReader();
     private final HandlerThread mHandlerThread;
     private final Handler mHandler;
@@ -138,8 +146,9 @@ public final class AxKernelManagerService {
     private void registerObserverForControl(KernelControlNode control) {
         if (control == null || TextUtils.isEmpty(control.id)) return;
         Uri uri = Settings.Secure.getUriFor(control.id);
-        if (uri == null) return;
+        if (uri == null || mObservedUris.contains(uri)) return;
         mResolver.registerContentObserver(uri, false, mSettingsObserver, UserHandle.USER_ALL);
+        mObservedUris.add(uri);
     }
 
     private void handleSettingChanged(Uri uri) {
@@ -201,6 +210,7 @@ public final class AxKernelManagerService {
         }
         mMetricsReader.setConfig(metricsConfig);
         publishMetadata(controls);
+        registerObserversLocked();
     }
 
